Debuting on January 12 and charting for 23 weeks, the single peaked at number five on the US [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] chart on April 13, 1974.<ref name="Hot 100 1974">{{Cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/charts/hot-100/1974-04-13|title=The Billboard Hot 100 |magazine=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]|access-date=August 8, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150304045027/https://www.billboard.com/charts/hot-100/1974-04-13/|archive-date=March 4, 2015|url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/charts/hot-100/1974-06-15/|title=The Billboard Hot 100|date=June 15, 1974|magazine=Billboard|access-date=August 9, 2025|archive-date=December 9, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241209162831/https://www.billboard.com/charts/hot-100/1974-06-15/|url-status=live}}</ref> The single was certified gold by the [[RIAA]] on April 22, 1974.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.riaa.com/gold-platinum/?tab_active=default-award&ar=redbone&ti=your+love&lab=&genre=&format=&date_option=release&from=&to=&award=&type=&category=&adv=SEARCH#search_section|title=Gold & Platinum|publisher=RIAA|access-date=August 8, 2025|archive-date=December 19, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251219075328/https://www.riaa.com/gold-platinum/?tab_active=default-award&ar=redbone&ti=your%20love&lab=&genre=&format=&date_option=release&from=&to=&award=&type=&category=&adv=SEARCH#search_section|url-status=live}}</ref> The song is Redbone's highest charting single and one of two Top 40 hits by the band. (An earlier recording, "[[The Witch Queen of New Orleans]]," peaked at number 21 in 1972.) 

In year-end charts, "Come and Get Your Love" ranked no. 4 on the [[Billboard Year-End Hot 100 singles of 1974|''Billboard'' Top Pop Singles of 1974]]<ref name="Billboard year-end 1974">{{cite magazine |title=Top Pop Singles |url=https://worldradiohistory.com/Archive-Billboard/70s/1974/Billboard%201974-12-28-II-Talent-in-Action.pdf |magazine=Billboard's Annual Talent in Action |publisher=Billboard Publications, Inc. |page=8 |date=December 28, 1974 |access-date=August 8, 2025 |archive-date=August 6, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200806213724/https://worldradiohistory.com/Archive-Billboard/70s/1974/Billboard%201974-12-28-II-Talent-in-Action.pdf |url-status=live }}</ref> and no. 33 on ''Broadcasting'' magazine's top 100 radio singles.<ref name="Broadcasting 1974"/>{{rp|36}}

